    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Constitutional authorities like the CAG, UPSC Chairman, and Chief Election Commissioner serve for a term of 6 years or until reaching 65 years of age, whichever is earlier.",
        "The retirement age for Supreme Court judges is 65 years, whereas for High Court judges, it is 62 years.",
        "The minimum age requirement to contest elections for President, Vice-President, and Governor is 35 years.",
        "The minimum age eligible to become a member of the Lok Sabha is 25 years, whereas for the Rajya Sabha, it is 30 years."
